                    {"type": "short", "stem": "Why is a file needed for a class list that must still be there after the program stops?", "answer": "Variables exist only while the program is running. A file stores the characters on disk so a later run, or another program, can read them."},
                    {"type": "short", "stem": "A file contains three names, each written with a newline. A student says the program 'printed blank lines between the names'. What is the likely cause?", "answer": "The loop kept the newline from the file and print added another. strip() on the line removes the file's newline."},
