                    {"type": "short", "stem": "Using the employees table in this lecture, what does `SELECT name FROM employees WHERE salary >= 80000 ORDER BY name;` return?", "answer": "Ayesha and Hina, in that order, because both have salary at least 80000 and Ayesha comes before Hina alphabetically. Bilal is excluded."},
                    {"type": "short", "stem": "Enrolment(StudentID, CourseID, StudentName, Grade) has key (StudentID, CourseID). Which normal form does it break, and what tables replace it?", "answer": "It breaks second normal form because StudentName depends only on StudentID. Replace it with Student(StudentID, StudentName) and Result(StudentID, CourseID, Grade)."},
